    "notes": "Labour force participation rate (LFPR) measures the share of the working-age population (15–64) that is either employed or actively looking for work. South Africa's LFPR is low by international standards, partly reflecting high rates of discouragement. NOTE (2026-10-19, data refresh): lfpr-overall and female-labour-participation were verified against QLFS P0211 tables (Q1 2025 and Q2 2026 releases) for Q1 2024–Q2 2026; the previously stored values for that window (e.g. 60.6% for Q4 2025 vs official 59.3%) did not match and were corrected. Points before Q1 2024 (lfpr-overall from Q1 2020; female from Q1 2022) were NOT re-verified. Per owner decision D1 (2026-10-23), the unverified 'labour-force-participation' (42.7%) record was removed from display and from this dataset.",
    "public_notes": "Labour force participation rate (LFPR) measures the share of the working-age population (15 to 64) that is either employed or actively looking for work. South Africa's LFPR is low by international standards, partly reflecting high rates of discouragement. Values from Q1 2024 to Q2 2026 were checked against Stats SA QLFS (P0211) tables. Earlier points have not yet been rechecked."
